[D] PRODUCT DEMO: self-converse tournament codec
    Use case: ranking systems with antisymmetric structure (round-robins,
    pairwise-preference matrices that are converse-symmetric under a known
    relabeling phi). Such a system's full pairwise matrix costs C(n,2) bits;
    the half-tiling fingerprint costs only half(n) ~ C(n,2)/2 bits.
    Example n=7: drew a random SC tournament.
      compressed fingerprint (half=9 bits): 101000100
      packed integer fingerprint: 69
      H (directed Hamiltonian paths) = 81
      full tiling would need m=15 bits; full adjacency C(7,2)=21 bits.
      canonical round-trip encode(decode(code))==code: True
    The global H-maximizer at n=7 (Paley T_7, H=189) is self-converse and
    thus lives in the codec's domain -- its fingerprint is a 9-bit code.

